<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karl Ludwig Sand</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1795">1795</a>–<a href="/years/1820">1820</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karl Ludwig Sand was a German theology student and member of the radical student fraternity movement who stabbed the conservative writer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/august-von-kotzebue">August von Kotzebue</a> to death in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mannheim">Mannheim</a> in March 1819. He was executed in 1820. Metternich used the murder to justify the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlsbad-decrees">Carlsbad Decrees</a>, which imposed censorship and supervision of the universities throughout the German Confederation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karl-ludwig-sand.jpg" alt="Karl Ludwig Sand" width="263" height="264" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karl_Ludwig_Sand_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
